+# Research consulted
+
+Accessed 2026-08-15. All entries below are live Broadcom publications consulted before implementing the plan; the pinned local snapshot remains the reproducible implementation authority.
+
+The exact evaluated paths were VMware Aria Operations 8.18.6 to VCF Operations 9.0.2, VMware Aria Automation 8.18.0 to VCF Automation 9.0.2, and VMware Aria Operations for Logs 8.18.3 to VCF Operations for Logs 9.0.1. The live publications establish the applicable release-family path, content limits, end of general support, sizing, and workload domain constraints; the snapshot pins the exact target patch and installer values where Broadcom's publication describes the 9.0.x family.
+
+| Broadcom publication | Reachable URL | Design claims informed |
+|---|---|---|
+| Upgrade of Aria Operations 8.18.6 or 8.18.7 to VCF Operations 9.0.x is Unsupported (Broadcom Knowledge Base 438994) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/438994 | A direct 8.18.6-to-9.0.x upgrade is unsafe and unsupported; use a greenfield 9.0.2 deployment, export/import dashboards, super metrics, views and reports, and do not claim historical time-series transfer. |
+| Import and upgrade VMware Aria Automation 8.x to VCF Automation 9.0 (Broadcom Knowledge Base 433806) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/433806/import-and-upgrade-vmware-aria-automatio.html | Import the existing Automation environment from Aria Suite Lifecycle into VCF Operations Fleet Management as an integrated instance before triggering the upgrade. |
+| Essential prechecks for a successful VCF Automation Upgrade (Broadcom Knowledge Base 389563) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/389563/essential-prechecks-for-a-successful-vcf.html | AVI cloud accounts and Kubernetes/TKG-era integrations are upgrade blockers; remove unsupported source features before the 9.0 upgrade. NSX Policy and vSphere accounts remain on the supported in-place route represented by the snapshot. |
+| Importing Aria Automation 8.x environment into VCF Fleet Manager is connecting to LCM and VC but not pulling up network data (Broadcom Knowledge Base 425169) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/425169/importing-aria-automation-8x-environment.html | Fleet import depends on the management/workload-domain database record for the vCenter that hosts Automation; complete workload-domain import before product import. |
+| Upgrade Guidance for Aria Operations for Logs 8.18.x to VCF Operations for Logs 9.0.x (Broadcom Knowledge Base 402314) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/402314 | Logs 8.18.x has no in-place path to 9.0.x; deploy fresh in parallel, unconfigure/reconfigure integrations, retain the old cluster for history, and transfer at most 90 days of log data. |
+| How to copy your Aria Operations for Logs from an existing installation to a new instance (Broadcom Knowledge Base 411801) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/411801/how-to-copy-your-aria-operations-for-log.html | Export/import My Content as VLCP; recreate secrets because encrypted credentials do not transfer; reconfigure agents, integrations and forwarding on a new cluster. |
